      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While staying hydrated is essential, drinking a ton of water alone may not be enough to offset the potential oxalate-related risks of high-dose vitamin C. Vitamin C can also increase the acidity of the urine, potentially increasing oxalate solubility and binding to calcium, which may worsen stone formation. Additionally, excessive vitamin C intake can lead to an imbalance of other essential nutrients and cause kidney strain. Moderation is key; consider consulting a healthcare professional to find a balance that meets your specific needs.",
